From: RobertGarciaa <chae0218@naver.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camera: Skip Qualcomm sensor mode table header in both searches

The first two integers are the row count and row stride. Start matching
width/height/FPS at offset two, as the existing (offset - 2)/stride + 1
mode-index calculation already expects. Do not force an arbitrary mode.

---
--- a/smali/com/oneplus/camera/hardware/camera2/wrappers/OPNormalCamcorderImpl.smali
+++ b/smali/com/oneplus/camera/hardware/camera2/wrappers/OPNormalCamcorderImpl.smali
@@ -4579,7 +4579,7 @@
 
     add-int/lit8 v13, v13, -0x3
 
-    invoke-direct {v12, v7, v13}, Lkotlin/ranges/IntRange;-><init>(II)V
+    invoke-direct {v12, v8, v13}, Lkotlin/ranges/IntRange;-><init>(II)V
 
     check-cast v12, Lkotlin/ranges/IntProgression;
 
@@ -4705,7 +4705,7 @@
 
     add-int/lit8 v11, v11, -0x3
 
-    const/4 v12, 0x0
+    const/4 v12, 0x2
 
     invoke-direct {v8, v12, v11}, Lkotlin/ranges/IntRange;-><init>(II)V
 
